WEBVTT

00:22.981 --> 00:24.858
DELICIOUS IN DUNGEON

01:41.309 --> 01:42.769
Really, though.

01:43.353 --> 01:46.565
There's nothing more horrifying
than black magic.

01:47.232 --> 01:50.110
Was bringing this person back
worth going down that path?

01:50.193 --> 01:52.612
It's only natural for Shuro to be furious.

01:53.155 --> 01:56.533
Using shady methods
like that to resurrect someone?

01:56.616 --> 01:58.368
That's just risky.

01:58.952 --> 02:01.079
Letting her stay dead
would've been better for her--

02:01.163 --> 02:02.122
Enough!

02:03.373 --> 02:05.208
I understand your point,

02:06.084 --> 02:07.544
so please stop.

02:10.589 --> 02:11.590
Sorry.

02:12.090 --> 02:15.552
Shuro, deep down, you probably know

02:16.219 --> 02:20.515
that if you were in his shoes,
you'd have done the same thing.

02:20.599 --> 02:21.850
I know that!

02:21.933 --> 02:24.895
But his attitude is just too much!

02:25.520 --> 02:26.938
We fed on monsters!

02:27.022 --> 02:29.566
I think my favorite is the Red Dragon
because of the memories.

02:29.649 --> 02:31.484
Check this out! It's a monster sword!

02:31.568 --> 02:35.322
We may have used black magic,
but you won't tell anyone, right?

02:36.364 --> 02:40.202
Anyway, I have no idea
what's going on in your head.

02:41.244 --> 02:42.746
I doubt I'll ever understand.

02:43.538 --> 02:44.748
So I can't help you.

02:45.457 --> 02:46.750
Laios! Senshi!

02:47.250 --> 02:48.418
We've got trouble!

02:48.501 --> 02:51.630
A group of monsters
is attacking the cooking crew and…

02:53.506 --> 02:54.424
What have you done?

02:55.050 --> 02:57.636
I told him everything
that's happened so far.

02:58.637 --> 02:59.638
Everything?!

02:59.721 --> 03:01.806
I thought that Shuro would understand.

03:01.890 --> 03:03.808
Shuro's the last person
you should have told!

03:03.892 --> 03:04.726
I figured.

03:04.809 --> 03:06.311
Is this on me?

03:06.394 --> 03:08.772
Did I make the wrong call?

03:09.272 --> 03:11.149
Don't beat yourself up.

03:11.232 --> 03:13.276
He's just a little tired.

03:15.570 --> 03:17.739
<i>I have a lot of respect for him.</i>

03:17.822 --> 03:21.534
<i>He's helped me out countless times
on our adventures.</i>

03:22.327 --> 03:25.288
<i>He told me tales of foreign lands</i>

03:25.372 --> 03:27.916
<i>when all I've known
was my homeland and this island.</i>

03:27.999 --> 03:31.544
<i>Shuro's always been cool-headed and smart.</i>

03:32.837 --> 03:35.257
For him to explode like that,

03:35.840 --> 03:38.051
I must've really messed up.

03:38.551 --> 03:41.972
It'd be a shame
if our friendship ended like this…

03:49.938 --> 03:50.814
Harpies.

03:54.693 --> 03:56.319
This is getting us nowhere.

03:56.403 --> 03:57.237
Asebi!

03:57.320 --> 03:58.530
Let's go, you three!

04:01.950 --> 04:05.745
Laios told Shuro everything
that's happened so far.

04:05.829 --> 04:08.081
What? Is that why the air is so tense?

04:08.164 --> 04:10.208
Shuro's furious.

04:10.292 --> 04:11.209
What do we do?

04:11.293 --> 04:13.003
If the story gets to the surface, we…

04:13.086 --> 04:16.006
I know! I know, but…

04:17.590 --> 04:20.510
It looks like the ninjas
are handling things just fine.

04:20.593 --> 04:23.179
Anyway, who else knows?

04:23.263 --> 04:24.431
Four people for now.

04:24.514 --> 04:26.599
Shuro and two of his retainers,

04:27.309 --> 04:29.269
and that curly-haired guy.

04:32.397 --> 04:35.775
He's the guy whose party
was wiped out by Treasure Bugs, right?

04:36.568 --> 04:38.069
What's he doing here?

04:38.153 --> 04:39.237
Who knows?

04:39.321 --> 04:42.907
Maybe he's after
whoever stole their loot and food.

04:42.991 --> 04:45.243
W-We have to clear that up!

04:45.327 --> 04:49.164
The loot was just Treasure Bugs
and the food was drenched and ruined!

04:49.247 --> 04:50.623
You idiot!

04:50.707 --> 04:53.251
The bigger problem
is your use of black magic.

04:53.835 --> 04:55.962
Shuro is angry, but he's not a concern.

04:56.671 --> 04:59.883
He's just ticked off
we put Falin in danger.

05:00.467 --> 05:02.344
But I'm not sure about the others.

05:03.219 --> 05:07.265
By the way, how much evidence
is left of you using black magic?

05:08.308 --> 05:11.686
The magic circle
got erased by the Cleaners,

05:11.770 --> 05:16.274
but there might be trouble if they check
Falin's body and my staff too closely.

05:16.358 --> 05:18.401
We need to torch your staff right now!

05:18.485 --> 05:19.569
Wait a minute!

05:19.652 --> 05:23.114
If they're already onto us that much,
burning my staff won't make a difference.

05:23.782 --> 05:24.991
Huh?

05:27.577 --> 05:28.536
Over there, look!

05:31.122 --> 05:32.999
What's that monster?

05:33.083 --> 05:34.042
A Harpy?

05:34.125 --> 05:35.418
No.

05:54.145 --> 05:55.105
What?

05:55.188 --> 05:56.064
No.

05:56.731 --> 05:57.565
No.

05:57.649 --> 05:58.566
How?

05:59.526 --> 06:00.568
Falin…

06:03.071 --> 06:03.947
It can't be.

06:06.157 --> 06:06.991
No.

06:08.493 --> 06:09.953
What on earth?

06:15.208 --> 06:17.585
<i>It's so cool!</i>

06:19.796 --> 06:21.881
<i>But it's a little too greedy.</i>

06:21.965 --> 06:24.342
<i>It's got wings, feathers, and scales too.</i>

06:24.425 --> 06:25.301
Falin!

06:25.802 --> 06:27.387
Do you recognize me?

06:27.470 --> 06:28.847
Knock it off, Marcille!

06:28.930 --> 06:30.098
Falin!

06:32.267 --> 06:34.435
-Holm! Rin! Prepare for battle!
-Falin!

06:34.519 --> 06:35.353
-R-Right!
-Right.

06:35.436 --> 06:37.689
-Laios, Shuro! What's the plan?
-Falin!

06:37.772 --> 06:38.815
Tell us what to do!

06:38.898 --> 06:41.192
Inutade, don't hurt her!

06:41.276 --> 06:42.694
Try to restrain her!

06:42.777 --> 06:44.195
Uh. Huh?

06:44.279 --> 06:46.531
No, Young Master. Run--

07:06.759 --> 07:08.761
So, I need to restrain her.

07:08.845 --> 07:10.638
Restrain her without hurting her.

07:10.722 --> 07:12.223
Restrain her without hurting her?

07:26.529 --> 07:27.655
Can you do it, Holm?

07:27.739 --> 07:28.948
Y-Yeah.

07:30.200 --> 07:31.367
All right.

07:31.451 --> 07:32.285
Come out.

07:55.266 --> 07:56.100
Falin!

07:56.184 --> 07:57.977
A-An Undine?

07:58.061 --> 07:59.812
Are you controlling that?

07:59.896 --> 08:01.356
Please make it stop!

08:01.439 --> 08:03.441
She's just confused.

08:05.026 --> 08:06.236
Give me a break.

08:06.778 --> 08:09.113
You don't care how many people die

08:09.197 --> 08:11.699
if you can protect someone
dear to you, is that it?

08:12.951 --> 08:14.702
That thing isn't "her."

08:15.286 --> 08:16.579
It's just a monster!

08:20.166 --> 08:23.086
<i>Ludeloes Arnbite.</i>

08:30.593 --> 08:32.595
Oh, Marillier…

08:32.679 --> 08:34.264
It can even cast spells?

08:48.611 --> 08:50.154
No, Kuro!

08:50.238 --> 08:51.656
Don't, you fool! Stay hidden!

08:54.826 --> 08:55.660
Falin…

09:01.624 --> 09:02.625
Out of my way!

09:03.293 --> 09:05.378
<i>Andarses Orbis!</i>

09:21.102 --> 09:22.854
<i>Monsters are dangerous.</i>

09:23.855 --> 09:25.189
<i>Damn it, Kensuke!</i>

09:25.273 --> 09:26.149
<i>Never trust a monster…</i>

09:30.403 --> 09:31.738
Forgive me, Falin.

09:32.363 --> 09:35.408
I wish I could've
switched places with you.

09:44.667 --> 09:46.419
My big brother, Laios.

09:57.639 --> 09:58.723
Falin!

09:58.806 --> 10:00.683
The lungs, kidneys,

10:01.517 --> 10:02.560
and the heart!

10:14.197 --> 10:15.406
<i>I'm going to die.</i>

10:18.618 --> 10:19.619
Can you stand?

10:20.244 --> 10:21.663
I'm sorry I hesitated.

10:21.746 --> 10:23.623
You're right.

10:23.706 --> 10:25.249
My sister's soul

10:25.333 --> 10:28.294
is probably under the control
of the lord of the dungeon now.

10:29.879 --> 10:33.091
But if we kill her,
the lunatic magician will show up again.

10:33.716 --> 10:35.677
For now, we need to get out of here.

10:36.260 --> 10:37.220
But--

10:47.230 --> 10:48.314
Falin!

10:50.400 --> 10:51.317
Hey!

10:56.531 --> 10:57.365
You monster!

10:57.448 --> 11:01.160
<i>Ludeloes Ejectulm Hemtum.</i>

11:01.828 --> 11:03.121
This spell…

11:03.204 --> 11:05.123
Everyone, stay close to me!

11:12.130 --> 11:13.214
Essiet!

11:41.826 --> 11:43.244
She might return.

11:43.327 --> 11:45.163
Let's get the wounded inside the barrier.

11:45.746 --> 11:47.206
And the dead…

11:47.290 --> 11:48.875
What should we do?

11:49.876 --> 11:51.502
I'll resurrect them.

11:52.003 --> 11:53.671
I can't revive everyone, though.

11:54.881 --> 11:56.507
Should I gather the bodies?

11:56.591 --> 11:58.843
No, don't move them.

11:58.926 --> 12:01.429
We can't waste a drop of shed blood.

12:05.475 --> 12:06.476
Where's the monster?!

12:06.559 --> 12:08.769
It bolted. We're safe now.

12:09.479 --> 12:10.521
Who's next?

12:10.605 --> 12:11.439
Wait.

12:11.522 --> 12:13.524
Bring back that woman first.

12:15.902 --> 12:17.028
Why me?

12:18.029 --> 12:20.948
You seemed to be a powerful mage.

12:21.032 --> 12:23.868
So I thought you could use
healing and resurrection magic.

12:24.452 --> 12:27.205
He can't heal everyone alone.

12:27.747 --> 12:31.375
You helped us get here,
so this is the least we can do.

12:31.459 --> 12:32.710
So now I owe you.

12:32.793 --> 12:34.879
My guess is
you're after a different spell.

12:35.671 --> 12:36.881
Never mind.

12:36.964 --> 12:38.216
Let us get this done quickly.

12:38.799 --> 12:41.302
Um, I can use
basic resurrection magic too.

12:41.385 --> 12:42.220
No.

12:42.803 --> 12:44.514
Don't you lay a finger on them.

12:45.139 --> 12:48.267
I can't let you use any more black magic.

12:49.185 --> 12:51.020
I-I wouldn't do that.

12:51.103 --> 12:52.605
Then what was that?

12:52.688 --> 12:54.649
Why did she look like that?

12:54.732 --> 12:57.985
It's because you used the Dragon's flesh
and black magic on her!

12:58.069 --> 13:00.029
No! That can't be!

13:00.112 --> 13:02.114
The magic didn't have that kind of power.

13:02.740 --> 13:05.701
B-But it's possible that

13:06.202 --> 13:09.539
the Red Dragon's soul
was under some spell.

13:10.289 --> 13:12.291
And Falin's soul merged with the Dragon's,

13:12.375 --> 13:15.169
and the lunatic magician
transformed her into that creature.

13:16.212 --> 13:17.380
Shuro?

13:17.463 --> 13:19.465
I'm handing Marcille over
to the elves of the west.

13:20.466 --> 13:22.426
I can't kill that thing.

13:22.510 --> 13:24.762
But I can't let it roam free either.

13:25.596 --> 13:28.516
I want to free her soul from the dungeon

13:28.599 --> 13:30.685
and let her rest in peace at least.

13:31.561 --> 13:32.520
But…

13:32.603 --> 13:34.730
The elves will know how to do that.

13:35.898 --> 13:38.776
Confess everything
to the elves of the west.

13:39.360 --> 13:40.444
No, Shuro.

13:40.528 --> 13:42.280
There has to be another way.

13:42.363 --> 13:43.614
Give me a break!

13:43.698 --> 13:45.783
What have you been doing until now?

13:45.866 --> 13:47.660
Another way?

13:47.743 --> 13:48.786
What's your plan?

13:49.328 --> 13:50.830
Are you going to keep resurrecting her

13:50.913 --> 13:53.457
with different monster parts
until she's back to normal?

13:54.375 --> 13:55.501
Go on, tell me!

13:55.585 --> 13:57.753
What are you going to do?

13:58.337 --> 13:59.505
You have an idea, don't you?

13:59.589 --> 14:00.881
Tell me!

14:06.637 --> 14:08.681
We'll defeat the lunatic magician!

14:09.265 --> 14:13.144
That Red Dragon
was clearly following orders.

14:13.227 --> 14:17.106
Who else but the magician who created
this dungeon could command it?

14:17.815 --> 14:21.360
So, we'll take down the magician
and rewrite his orders!

14:21.861 --> 14:24.071
I'm not familiar with this sort of thing,

14:24.655 --> 14:26.490
but Marcille should know how!

14:26.574 --> 14:28.284
That's why I won't let you take her!

14:28.784 --> 14:30.953
I've had enough!

14:31.037 --> 14:35.333
Are you really going to use black magic
to fix a problem caused by black magic?

14:35.416 --> 14:37.752
Why don't you start
taking things seriously for once?

14:44.926 --> 14:46.093
Uh… sorr--

14:54.268 --> 14:57.521
It's true I'm not the most skilled,

14:57.605 --> 15:00.107
and you're stronger than most adventurers.

15:01.025 --> 15:03.986
But here's what I know.

15:04.820 --> 15:06.864
We've been getting
proper meals three times a day

15:06.948 --> 15:08.491
and good sleep too.

15:08.574 --> 15:10.284
That makes us more serious than you!

15:11.327 --> 15:12.328
Listen to me!

15:12.411 --> 15:17.708
We will take down the lunatic magician
and rescue Falin, no matter what!

15:17.792 --> 15:20.378
Shuro, you go back to the surface.

15:20.461 --> 15:23.381
Eat, bathe, and rest!

15:27.093 --> 15:28.594
Huh? What was that?

15:30.012 --> 15:32.848
Shut up!

15:34.767 --> 15:37.103
The fight isn't over yet.

15:37.186 --> 15:40.856
If that's your plan, I have one of my own.

15:40.940 --> 15:41.899
Plan?

15:43.109 --> 15:44.360
Laios!

15:44.443 --> 15:45.486
Listen up.

15:46.070 --> 15:47.446
For a long time now,

15:48.155 --> 15:50.658
I couldn't stand your guts.

15:51.283 --> 15:54.161
Because you were thoughtless, dense,

15:54.245 --> 15:55.621
<i>and always had the worst timing!</i>

15:55.705 --> 15:57.540
Hey, tell me more
about those foreign lands!

15:57.623 --> 15:59.959
Are you two eating together? Count me in!

16:00.042 --> 16:02.086
We're friends now, right?

16:02.169 --> 16:05.256
<i>It was even worse
because you meant no harm!</i>

16:05.339 --> 16:07.550
Why don't I just end you here,

16:07.633 --> 16:08.884
take Marcille, and--

16:08.968 --> 16:10.594
Well, you should've told me sooner!

16:10.678 --> 16:12.596
Why were you keeping quiet until now

16:12.680 --> 16:16.642
if you couldn't stand me and thought
I was dense and had terrible timing?

16:16.726 --> 16:20.146
I was dropping hints
that most people would've picked up on!

16:20.896 --> 16:23.524
You should've made
more of an effort to notice!

16:23.607 --> 16:24.525
How could I?

16:24.608 --> 16:28.029
You were the first friend
I made on this island,

16:28.112 --> 16:30.823
and I was too excited to realize!

16:30.906 --> 16:34.618
See, that's another thing
I can't stand about you!

16:34.702 --> 16:36.704
You act all honest

16:36.787 --> 16:38.831
but end up stressing people out!

16:39.832 --> 16:41.333
How was I supposed to know?

16:41.917 --> 16:44.253
You never speak up and you don't even eat!

16:44.336 --> 16:47.548
What's the point of having a mouth?

16:47.631 --> 16:49.300
Shut up, you moron!

16:49.383 --> 16:52.595
You haven't put in
half the effort Marcille has.

16:52.678 --> 16:54.805
We don't have time for this.

16:54.889 --> 16:56.640
It's a childish squabble.

16:57.266 --> 16:59.393
I must have raised him wrong.

17:00.436 --> 17:02.521
Seven dead, including myself,

17:02.605 --> 17:05.232
one in critical condition,
and three missing.

17:06.275 --> 17:09.653
The gnome and I will resurrect them,
but we're low on blood.

17:10.362 --> 17:13.282
Senshi, can you gather
the scattered ingredients?

17:13.783 --> 17:14.909
Sure.

17:14.992 --> 17:17.578
I can use basic resurrection magic too.

17:17.661 --> 17:19.455
You stay out of this.

17:22.500 --> 17:26.045
Heal the wounded and find the missing.

17:26.128 --> 17:28.714
If you try anything suspicious,
I'll cut you down on the spot.

17:54.490 --> 17:55.825
See, Shuro?

17:56.408 --> 17:59.245
Right now, I'm better fed than you are.

17:59.328 --> 18:00.579
That's why I'm stronger!

18:00.663 --> 18:02.373
D-Damn it.

18:16.804 --> 18:17.721
It's good.

18:18.681 --> 18:21.475
Young Master, we've resurrected everyone.

18:22.059 --> 18:24.145
When do you wish to depart?

18:25.521 --> 18:28.107
No, prepare the return magic.

18:28.190 --> 18:29.191
We're heading back up.

18:29.775 --> 18:31.026
Are you sure?

18:31.861 --> 18:33.863
Asebi is still missing.

18:33.946 --> 18:35.072
She probably ran off.

18:35.156 --> 18:35.990
Let her be.

18:36.490 --> 18:39.702
Please forgive our inadequacy.

18:40.244 --> 18:41.120
No.

18:41.203 --> 18:43.497
You did your best.

18:44.373 --> 18:45.499
Thank you.

18:45.583 --> 18:47.585
I'm sorry for dragging you into this.

18:52.590 --> 18:54.008
I'm returning to my homeland.

18:55.134 --> 18:56.969
I'll never set foot on this island again.

18:58.596 --> 19:01.348
I'll report what happened
to the Lord of the Island.

19:02.349 --> 19:03.517
I see.

19:04.685 --> 19:06.687
I wish I could've returned with Falin.

19:07.605 --> 19:09.773
What was her answer to your proposal?

19:09.857 --> 19:10.774
I don't know.

19:12.151 --> 19:14.403
She said she needed time
to think about it.

19:15.321 --> 19:16.530
I was waiting for her answer.

19:25.039 --> 19:27.791
<i>There's no woman
more fascinating than her.</i>

19:29.501 --> 19:32.630
<i>I loved her voice, the way she thought,</i>

19:34.340 --> 19:35.716
<i>and her smile.</i>

19:39.053 --> 19:43.015
But I never actually
brought any of this up with her.

19:44.516 --> 19:46.310
I wish I had told her sooner.

19:47.478 --> 19:50.189
Wait, so he just popped
the question out of nowhere?

19:50.272 --> 19:51.440
That's scary.

19:51.523 --> 19:53.234
From where he comes from, it's normal.

19:53.734 --> 19:56.820
I see. Well, I'll pass on
your words to Falin.

20:00.783 --> 20:02.826
That's the part about you

20:05.120 --> 20:06.163
that I envy.

20:09.375 --> 20:12.711
Kabru, you were a big help.

20:12.795 --> 20:14.129
I didn't do much.

20:14.213 --> 20:16.048
My attack ended up being useless.

20:16.131 --> 20:18.884
No, it helped me notice
a couple of things.

20:18.968 --> 20:20.219
Like what?

20:20.302 --> 20:23.305
The places you stabbed
would've been fatal for a human,

20:23.389 --> 20:25.224
but not for my sister.

20:25.766 --> 20:28.686
This means either that
she doesn't have vital organs there,

20:28.769 --> 20:30.437
or she has more somewhere else.

20:31.021 --> 20:35.901
A bunch of monsters like the Basilisk,
Cerberus, and Scylla have multiple brains.

20:35.985 --> 20:38.195
It's pretty common in Chimera types.

20:39.154 --> 20:41.031
<i>His pupils are dilated.</i>

20:41.615 --> 20:43.284
<i>He must really love monsters.</i>

20:43.993 --> 20:45.703
<i>So his knowledge is his weapon.</i>

20:45.786 --> 20:48.455
<i>He says he'll defeat the lunatic magician.</i>

20:48.539 --> 20:51.917
<i>There are plenty of adventurers
more skilled than him,</i>

20:52.001 --> 20:55.087
<i>but none with his level
of knowledge and motivation.</i>

20:56.046 --> 20:58.465
<i>This guy might just pull it off.</i>

20:59.967 --> 21:00.843
<i>But</i>

21:01.552 --> 21:04.054
<i>what happens after he defeats
the lord of the dungeon?</i>

21:04.138 --> 21:06.432
<i>They say whoever
takes down the lunatic magician</i>

21:06.515 --> 21:08.851
<i>will gain everything in the kingdom.</i>

21:10.019 --> 21:14.148
<i>What if that means becoming
the next lord of the dungeon?</i>

21:15.399 --> 21:19.695
<i>What will he do with this city built
by black magic and all its monsters</i>

21:19.778 --> 21:21.113
<i>when he inherits them?</i>

21:21.655 --> 21:24.241
<i>Will he quietly seal the dungeon?</i>

21:25.409 --> 21:26.702
Aren't you hungry?

21:26.785 --> 21:27.786
Huh?

21:42.301 --> 21:46.638
HARPY EGG OMELET

21:47.890 --> 21:49.308
What's this?

21:49.391 --> 21:51.727
It's an omelet made from a Harpy egg.

21:53.437 --> 21:56.190
Senshi found an egg earlier.

21:56.273 --> 21:58.525
You seemed interested in monster cuisine,

21:58.609 --> 22:00.110
so have one.

22:04.573 --> 22:06.116
<i>Mother!</i>

22:06.700 --> 22:08.619
<i>I'd rather die than eat it!</i>

22:09.203 --> 22:10.954
<i>What do I do? How do I get out of this?</i>

22:11.038 --> 22:14.083
<i>No, maybe I have no choice
but to kill him now.</i>

22:14.708 --> 22:15.667
<i>Not now!</i>

22:15.751 --> 22:16.752
I'll try one!

22:16.835 --> 22:18.087
<i>Typical of Kabru.</i>

22:18.170 --> 22:21.465
<i>He'll do anything to win someone's favor.</i>

22:21.548 --> 22:23.092
<i>What a nice guy.</i>

22:35.604 --> 22:38.607
The return magic is ready.

22:39.233 --> 22:41.276
No one is injured, yes?

22:41.360 --> 22:42.736
Beyond this portal is the surface.

22:42.820 --> 22:44.530
If you die there, we can't bring you back.

22:45.114 --> 22:46.448
To be honest,

22:46.532 --> 22:50.410
I think you'll die before you
even get to the lunatic magician.

22:51.120 --> 22:53.038
But if you do manage to survive,

22:53.580 --> 22:56.792
but can't make it back to the surface
because of black magic,

22:58.043 --> 22:59.044
ring this bell.

22:59.920 --> 23:02.297
It'll resonate with its twin far away.

23:02.840 --> 23:06.552
I'll send an escort
to help you flee to the east.

23:08.387 --> 23:09.346
Don't die.

23:10.931 --> 23:11.807
Thanks.

23:13.809 --> 23:14.685
Laios,

23:15.269 --> 23:16.436
I'm glad we got to chat.

23:16.520 --> 23:18.313
That was the highlight
of this trip for me.

23:18.814 --> 23:19.815
The pleasure is mine.

23:20.315 --> 23:21.441
Um…

23:21.525 --> 23:22.776
Quickly now.

23:22.860 --> 23:25.654
You remember my name now, right?

23:25.737 --> 23:27.406
Huh? Of course.

23:27.906 --> 23:28.782
Good.

23:30.409 --> 23:32.286
Don't forget next time.

23:33.829 --> 23:35.289
Well, see you.

23:36.582 --> 23:37.416
<i>Next time?</i>

23:38.834 --> 23:40.210
Let's go, Laios!

23:40.294 --> 23:42.504
There's no turning back now.

23:43.422 --> 23:45.215
Crap. See?

23:45.299 --> 23:48.385
I just knew this was going
to happen in the end.

23:48.468 --> 23:49.344
Crap!

23:49.887 --> 23:51.430
That's vulgar, Chil.

23:52.181 --> 23:53.098
I'm sorry.

23:56.894 --> 23:58.145
It'll all work out somehow.

25:30.070 --> 25:31.905
Subtitle translation by: Ai Matsuoka
